VERSION = "v0.34.0"
RELEASE_NOTE = "HA reliability release. Adds: (1) Readmit for nodes in 'failed' status, not just 'fenced' — a host the HA engine flagged failed that then recovers can be returned to service from the UI. (2) A readmit short-circuit that skips the Ceph fence-check when nothing was relocated off the node, so recovering a false-positive 'failed' host does not require HA_CEPH_KEY. (3) A mass-failure circuit breaker: if a large fraction of HA-eligible nodes go stale in the same heartbeat cycle (tunable via HA_MASS_FAILURE_FRACTION / HA_MASS_FAILURE_MIN), the engine treats it as a controller-side fault and suppresses flagging instead of downing the whole fleet. (4) Automatic recovery: a node flagged 'failed' is cleared back to 'online' automatically once it heartbeats again (fenced nodes still require guarded admin readmit). (5) Network-catalog auto-discovery: a periodic task imports OVS VLAN bridges found on the nodes into the networks catalog as hidden/admin-review."
